Prerequisite:
Check system time is Correct.
    # timedatectl or date
If system time is correct then proceed with Step 1
1) Install chrony package
    #dnf install chrony -y
2) Start and enable chronyd service
   # Systemctl enable chronyd --now
   # systemctl status chronyd
4) Edit chrony configuration file
   # vi /etc/chrony.conf
   allow <Network address.0>/subnet    (like here under)
   allow 192.168.100.0/24
save&quit
5) Restart chronyd service
   # systemctl restart chronyd
6) Open Firewall rules
   # firewall-cmd --add-port={123/udp,323/udp} --permanent
   # firewall-cmd --reload
   # firewall-cmd --add-service={ntp,ptp} --permanent
   # firewall-cmd --reload
7) Test if any clients are connected 
   # chronyc clients  -v     (there are no client connected, ll do client side setup now)
   # timedatectl
